Well, that was completely horrible. By the time it ended I was almost glad,
it was so painful.

Evil Overlord was the first of my Chaotic Wizards to begin his descent. In
the past (many years ago), I used to play Wizards as a sort of joke, since I
simply could not get them anywhere. Indeed, I would number them from Evil
Overlord I to about, oh, say XXXVI. With my recent (and first/only)
Ascension of a Valk, I figured hey, let's give a Wizard a try.

This time was a bit different. I had an almost easy time with the early
game. I used everything I had to the fullest, ran from dangerous encounters,
carefully prepared levels by digging routes between stairs, set up stashes,
moved spellbooks and other useful items deeper and deeper into the dungeon,
carefully used my pet to id cursed items, wore proper equipment, used lots
of thrown weapons, carefully id'd scrolls to find identify, didn't do
anything risky (drinking from fountains etc).

I progressed slowly and steadily through the early and midgame, gaining
levels, gathering spellbooks and spells, clearing the quest, Ludios, the
Castle, and then carefully preparing my gear for the descent into Heck^2
(not Gehennom this time :)). I had a blessed bag of holding with various
useful items, holy and unholy water etc. I had backup scrolls of genocide,
potions of full healing, scrolls of teleport, wands of teleport and digging,
a set of useful tools, +2 Magicbane, a full set of useful spells (except
Finger of Death). I spent a LONG time sacrificing to my god trying to get
useful items - he gave me Magicbane and that was it. No spellbooks, other
artifacts, no crowing from prayer, zippo. Many many wands of create monster,
bags of tricks, scrolls of create monster, hanging around on the level, etc,
nothing seemed to help. I polypiled useful items, gathered backup equipment
in my bag and on stashes on various floors of the dungeon. I utilized Charm
Monster, acquired pets, a magic whistle, a leash, outfitted them with useful
gear, brought them with me along the way. I tried nurse dancing for the
first time, and tried polymorphing into a Xorn and eating rings and amulets
for the first time as well, picking up a bunch of extra hp and useful
intrinsics. I had my ac below -40, str at 18/70 or so, all other stats at
18. I brought along four or five amulets of life saving. I genocided h, L,
;, c.

I fully magic mapped and treasure detected every floor from the top to the
bottom, dug out routes between stairs in Heck on every floor, dropped the
invocation tools on the vibrating square before going up to face the wizard.
I finally went to tackle the Wizard, zapped him with a wand of death
(missed, missed, missed), beat him down, killed him and took the Book. Went
down, activated the staircase, grabbed the Amulet, and started my ascent.

This is where things started to go very, very, VERY wrong. First, as I have
never played a caster class before, I did not know the Amulet of Yendor
drained mana when casting spells. That's bad. I did not have Finger of Death
or a good weapon (my best weapon other than the Magicbane was a +6
quarterstaff, my starting weapon!), so I could not kill him quickly with
spells or in melee. Then he steals the amulet (expected) and my artifact
(also expected). The Wizard proves to be remarkably resilient. I could not
blast him with spells, as my mana would run down. Magicbane would not dent
him, as it was doing too little damage, and he was hurting me pretty badly,
particularly when he double troubled. Once my artifact was stolen, he would
be resistant to my spells as well (and my energy regen was too slow to put a
dent in him). I wound up mired in combat with the Wizard, without making any
upwards progress through the depths at all - when I did manage to kill him
and retrieve the Amulet, I'd get pulled back down repeatedly, and by the
time I'd make it up again, the Wizard would resurrect, double trouble, steal
the items, and start the mess all over again.

Trying to figure out some way to kill him more quickly, I hesitantly
switched out to my quarterstaff, as I was concerned about his cursing.
Naturally, he cursed my staff immediately. Beh. Cast remove curse. 'You need
a hand free'. Um. Remember when I said I hadn't played a caster before?
Sigh. Alright, get a scroll of remove curse or holy water out of my Bag of
Holding. 'You need a hand free'. You must be kidding me. I couldn't pray
either, being in Gehennom, and was below Vlads (I believe you can pray
safely in there?). Didn't have any others in my inventory, none on the floor
on any floor (remember, I cleared every floor out carefully, so no free
items). I tried killing random creatures to get a drop, no such luck,
particularly with the Wiz resurrecting and re-attacking me so quickly.

At this point my situation was even worse. I couldn't ascend safely with the
Wizard hounding me, I couldn't uncurse my staff, couldn't cast spells,
couldn't access my bag. I finally managed to take the Wizard down using
conflict and all of my wands plus bashing him with the staff. I recovered my
artifact, and deliberately left the amulet behind. I level teleported out of
the depths, to return to one of my stashes and recouperate. I went to an
altar, sacrificed repeatedly until I saw a clover leaf, then prayed. God
displeased, no uncursing. Sigh. Can't access wands of create monster (in
bag), cursed conflict is making peaceful priest beat on me. I'll back off
for a bit, go look for some other stuff in the dungeon. Have ONE potion in
inventory (rest long since used up during super lengthy battles with Wiz or
stuck in bag). Maybe turn it into holy water. Go up a bit poking around for
a fountain. Ah, there's one. Walk over to it. Fire trap. Potion boils.
You've gotta be kidding me.

Ok, gotta go look for another potion or scroll or something. Black light
explodes. Beh, apply unicorn horn. Sicken, die. Yay.

It was uncursed before then, but I was still getting the 'malignant aura'
still (what causes this? is this an effect of acquiring the amulet of
yendor, and stays with you for the rest of the game from that point on?).

Anyhow. Never again am I going down to fight him without something stronger.
Fighting him with melee characters has always been a snap, I figured
blasting him with my wizard and my free pets would be even easier (get him
my pets! - hah, charm monster). Sadly, not knowing about the Amulet of
Yendor's mana drain made that an unusable strategy. I didn't account for
this in my planning, but I DID make serious efforts to acquire a better
weapon than Magicbane, in case it didn't work for some other reason. That
never panned out. I also did not know about what happens as a caster/with
bags if you get cursed with a two handed weapon. Never using one of those
again either. I'll keep backup holy water and remove cursed in my inventory
and stashed in various places near the stairs along the way up as well.

Don't think I've ever had a Nethack experience as frustrating and drawn out
as this :( I thought I had prepared more than adaquetely, apparently I was
wrong.



